WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.430
Within hypervisors, we have virtual machines.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.711
Virtual machines are software-based, fully
functional instances of an operating system

00:00:08.711 --> 00:00:15.040
inside a hypervisor, allowing us to run multiple
operating systems in one.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:21.050
Just for an example, I have two virtual machines
here: one Linux and one Windows.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.540
Each serves a specific purpose.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:30.180
The Linux virtual machine is here so that
I do not need a separate machine to run Linux.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.260
This instance of Windows is a test machine
that I can use to test things without running

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.739
tests on my regular operating system.

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:42.460
That is another reason for having a virtual:
to have a place to test apps and features

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.530
without risking one's regular operating system.

